01:11:28.100 --> 01:11:46.309
Dr. Karan Mittal: I have certain beliefs about following certain principles, spiritual and religious principles. And people who don't follow it, I look at them in a judgmental way. I look at them as inferiors, I look at them as not disciplined. So, does that belief make you look at others as inferior?

448
01:11:46.960 --> 01:12:02.960
Dr. Karan Mittal: does it produce an inner experience, or really outer compliance, like what we discussed in Jung and religion? That… is that belief really helping you transform within, or you're now just doing it mechanically as a compliance thing, and then feeling superior about following those principles?

449
01:12:03.260 --> 01:12:07.290
Dr. Karan Mittal: And could I still hold it without a group reinforcement? So if you were not

