01:16:35.960 --> 01:16:43.899
GOVINDA Das: You take many traditions. In fact, in one aspect of Christianity, It is seen as…

489
01:16:44.330 --> 01:16:47.999
GOVINDA Das: The birth of a woman itself is a mistake.

490
01:16:49.490 --> 01:16:51.569
GOVINDA Das: No? It is seen as a mistake.

491
01:16:52.640 --> 01:17:00.780
GOVINDA Das: Another tradition, when somebody's… Lame, somebody's tum, somebody's blind.

492
01:17:00.890 --> 01:17:04.149
GOVINDA Das: It is considered as fractured soul.

493
01:17:05.020 --> 01:17:08.950
GOVINDA Das: Just like the body is fractured, similarly, the soul is fractured.

494
01:17:10.370 --> 01:17:17.330
GOVINDA Das: And there are some traditions, they say, you know, some souls will perpetually rot in hell.

495
01:17:17.540 --> 01:17:21.780
GOVINDA Das: And some soul will perpetually go to the spiritual realm.

496
01:17:21.880 --> 01:17:27.649
GOVINDA Das: I remember reading some comment on, when Divine Comedy came out.

497
01:17:28.790 --> 01:17:35.979
GOVINDA Das: Dante, he wrote that book. He had a great appreciation for Socrates.

498
01:17:36.360 --> 01:17:39.290
GOVINDA Das: But Socrates came before Jesus Christ.

499
01:17:39.420 --> 01:17:41.520
GOVINDA Das: Now, where do you send Socrates?

500
01:17:42.600 --> 01:17:47.229
GOVINDA Das: Right? You cannot achieve perfection without the grace of Jesus.

501
01:17:48.240 --> 01:17:56.100
GOVINDA Das: But at the same time, you're such an infatu- in such an impact about Socrates, you don't want to send him to hellish planet.

502
01:17:57.180 --> 01:17:59.539
GOVINDA Das: So then there was a divine purgative.

503
01:17:59.910 --> 01:18:06.870
GOVINDA Das: Right? There was some neutral system was created, neither hell or nor heaven.

504
01:18:07.450 --> 01:18:11.660
GOVINDA Das: Otherwise, in this tradition, there are only two things. You go to hell, or you go to heaven.

505
01:18:13.680 --> 01:18:21.640
GOVINDA Das: So, therefore, The… the theology of mind is extremely abstract.

506
01:18:21.900 --> 01:18:25.049
GOVINDA Das: The religious beliefs are extremely concrete.

507
01:18:25.700 --> 01:18:31.089
GOVINDA Das: Believes are concrete, but the definition of mind is extremely abstract and confusing.

508
01:18:31.380 --> 01:18:37.190
GOVINDA Das: The brain is revered, but not back. Honored, not understood.

509
01:18:37.840 --> 01:18:41.939
GOVINDA Das: Mental illness is often reduced to sin, possession, or destiny.

510
01:18:42.860 --> 01:18:55.470
GOVINDA Das: Moral categories, not functional ones. As I said this, this was one of the greatest tragedy created in the… eventually, now it is… Europe is very progressive, but in those times.

511
01:18:55.970 --> 01:19:01.799
GOVINDA Das: Any kind of mental health was considered as proper, and here, sin.

512
01:19:02.120 --> 01:19:07.230
GOVINDA Das: Is basically, unless you take shelter of faith.

513
01:19:07.380 --> 01:19:12.330
GOVINDA Das: You cannot heal. But the problem is, if you have a… if you have a dental pain.

514
01:19:13.210 --> 01:19:18.470
GOVINDA Das: It doesn't matter how sincerely you take to the path of spirituality.

515
01:19:19.930 --> 01:19:22.280
GOVINDA Das: You cannot overcome that pain.

516
01:19:22.680 --> 01:19:30.290
GOVINDA Das: Mind is also matter, like a tooth only, but much more subtle, as Karan was mentioning.

517
01:19:30.850 --> 01:19:34.420
GOVINDA Das: Sometime you may have… you may have to separately deal with the mine.

518
01:19:34.840 --> 01:19:38.749
GOVINDA Das: Sometime you have to deal with, on a physical level.

519
01:19:39.440 --> 01:19:42.779
GOVINDA Das: And sometime you have to deal with a neurological damage.

520
01:19:51.610 --> 01:19:53.549
GOVINDA Das: Now, this is very important.

521
01:19:53.800 --> 01:19:54.780
GOVINDA Das: Alright?

522
01:19:54.950 --> 01:20:00.450
GOVINDA Das: The whole foundation of Indic knowledge lies on these three principles.

523
01:20:01.990 --> 01:20:04.870
GOVINDA Das: Satya Dharma Rutta.

524
01:20:05.050 --> 01:20:06.669
GOVINDA Das: And there is Sharata.

525
01:20:08.410 --> 01:20:14.000
GOVINDA Das: In the Bhagavatam Third Kento, there is a beautiful explanation of marriage of Dharma.

526
01:20:16.030 --> 01:20:21.820
GOVINDA Das: When Dharma is married to Shraddha, what does it do? It gives rise to auspiciousness.

527
01:20:23.480 --> 01:20:34.809
GOVINDA Das: If Dharma is not married to Sharadha, if Sharadha is not married to Dharma, what does it do? Dharma without Sharadha gives rise to inauspiciousness.

528
01:20:35.270 --> 01:20:45.909
GOVINDA Das: It gives rise to violence. It gives rise to separatism. It gives rise to one of the saddest parts. I remember I was attending an interfaith conference.

529
01:20:47.470 --> 01:20:50.440
GOVINDA Das: And those are devout spiritualists.

530
01:20:50.880 --> 01:20:54.939
GOVINDA Das: If you ask them this question, what is greater? Your faith is greater?

531
01:20:55.260 --> 01:21:00.769
GOVINDA Das: or your nation is greater.

532
01:21:04.130 --> 01:21:09.749
GOVINDA Das: what do they say? Generally, they say, no, we don't care for Rashtra. For us, faith is greater.

533
01:21:11.300 --> 01:21:17.509
GOVINDA Das: But if you study carefully, the Hindu scripture, there is no contradiction.

534
01:21:18.080 --> 01:21:21.210
GOVINDA Das: Faith is my inner journey.

535
01:21:21.960 --> 01:21:28.230
GOVINDA Das: And Rastra is my external loyalty. They are not in contradiction to each other.

536
01:21:28.770 --> 01:21:42.739
GOVINDA Das: I don't have to create a contradiction between the two. Therefore, the question is, what is Dharma? You know, if anybody wants to, in one sentence, you know, whatever you understand, what is Dharma is?

537
01:21:43.160 --> 01:21:48.089
GOVINDA Das: As I said, Dharma is not faith. Dharma is not ritual. Dharma is not belief.

538
01:21:49.090 --> 01:21:52.440
GOVINDA Das: Because this is the foundation of Indian knowledge system.

539
01:21:52.980 --> 01:21:56.740
GOVINDA Das: Dharma, Shraddha, Satya, and Rhuta.

540
01:21:57.420 --> 01:21:58.960
GOVINDA Das: And especially Daraba.

541
01:22:00.950 --> 01:22:07.019
GOVINDA Das: Now, those who have some understanding some assumption about Dharba.

542
01:22:07.460 --> 01:22:10.090
GOVINDA Das: Now, what do you think about what is Dharma?

543
01:22:10.280 --> 01:22:11.629
Lavina Shewaramani: Abush, can I say?

544
01:22:12.400 --> 01:22:13.200
Lavina Shewaramani: Yes?

545
01:22:13.400 --> 01:22:14.350
GOVINDA Das: Love energy?

546
01:22:14.350 --> 01:22:15.060
Lavina Shewaramani: Right.

547
01:22:15.540 --> 01:22:18.200
Lavina Shewaramani: Doing the right thing. Righteousness.

548
01:22:18.200 --> 01:22:19.100
GOVINDA Das: Doing the right.

549
01:22:19.460 --> 01:22:22.150
GOVINDA Das: Okay, doing righteousness.

550
01:22:22.150 --> 01:22:24.579
Aarti Ganesh: That doesn't change with circumstance.

551
01:22:25.330 --> 01:22:26.120
GOVINDA Das: Okay.

552
01:22:26.540 --> 01:22:29.319
shubham singh: Term is the eternal law… eternal law and order.

553
01:22:29.570 --> 01:22:32.279
GOVINDA Das: Eternal Land Auto, yes.

554
01:22:32.630 --> 01:22:34.640
GOVINDA Das: Yes? Anything else?

555
01:22:35.380 --> 01:22:38.270
suraj racha: The most navigable order in which one can function.

556
01:22:38.540 --> 01:22:39.850
GOVINDA Das: Aji, what is that?

557
01:22:39.850 --> 01:22:41.589
suraj racha: The most natural order.

558
01:22:42.070 --> 01:22:44.840
suraj racha: Universal natural order in which one can function.

559
01:22:45.100 --> 01:22:45.860
GOVINDA Das: Yeah.

560
01:22:46.150 --> 01:22:48.730
GOVINDA Das: So, all… all answers are right.

561
01:22:49.120 --> 01:22:50.030
GOVINDA Das: Right?

562
01:22:50.820 --> 01:22:58.149
GOVINDA Das: But when you study deeply, generally what happens, we consider our belief system as the greatest dharma.

563
01:22:59.150 --> 01:23:01.279
GOVINDA Das: We all give these different answers.

564
01:23:01.490 --> 01:23:16.779
GOVINDA Das: But generally, when we interact with the people, especially if you're a spiritual practitioner, your belief becomes the highest dharma, at the cost of isolating everyone, everybody else having a different belief system.

565
01:23:17.610 --> 01:23:22.780
GOVINDA Das: So, we make Dharma synonymous to belief system, so let us try to understand.

566
01:23:23.850 --> 01:23:26.809
GOVINDA Das: Not everything in Indian thought depends on belief.

567
01:23:27.490 --> 01:23:36.410
GOVINDA Das: In fact, we do not begin with belief. We begin with Dharma. What is that? Dharma is the natural laws of life.

568
01:23:37.180 --> 01:23:38.800
GOVINDA Das: unchangeable.

569
01:23:39.180 --> 01:23:40.190
GOVINDA Das: Right?

570
01:23:40.640 --> 01:23:45.500
GOVINDA Das: Shraddha is a personal conviction, very subjective.

571
01:23:46.690 --> 01:23:57.580
GOVINDA Das: I remember talking to about 50 students, On the day of Janmastery, Alright, so… the question was…

572
01:23:58.460 --> 01:24:02.570
GOVINDA Das: whether do I believe Krishna existed or not?

573
01:24:05.930 --> 01:24:10.579
GOVINDA Das: If they say, I don't believe Krishna existed, I said, can you prove that?

574
01:24:12.050 --> 01:24:21.169
GOVINDA Das: They said, we cannot prove, just like you cannot prove the existence of God, specifically Krishna Ram. How do you prove?

575
01:24:22.710 --> 01:24:28.650
GOVINDA Das: The judgment given by the court in regards to Raham Temple, that…

576
01:24:28.990 --> 01:24:33.339
GOVINDA Das: They did not say this was the birthplace of Lord Ram.

577
01:24:33.570 --> 01:24:41.399
GOVINDA Das: Because you cannot prove There are no hard artifacts to prove that this is the place of Lord Ra.

578
01:24:41.940 --> 01:24:46.070
GOVINDA Das: If you refer to the scripture, you cannot prove the…

579
01:24:46.210 --> 01:24:55.709
GOVINDA Das: the… the direct protection perman of the scriptures. So what happens then? Then I need to believe. A Mary Shaddahai, it is my faith.

580
01:24:55.920 --> 01:25:03.250
GOVINDA Das: The judge gave the judgment based upon Temple existed before the mosque.

581
01:25:03.700 --> 01:25:07.300
GOVINDA Das: Not because it was a birth pledge, because according to the Bhagavatam.

582
01:25:07.420 --> 01:25:14.339
GOVINDA Das: When Lord Ramachandra went back to the spiritual world, the entire Ayutthhya went into the waters.

583
01:25:15.090 --> 01:25:18.059
GOVINDA Das: Just like Dwarka went into the waters.

584
01:25:19.330 --> 01:25:23.319
GOVINDA Das: So, therefore, a shraddha is what I believe.

585
01:25:23.430 --> 01:25:28.419
GOVINDA Das: For me, my God, Krishna, Lord Ram, Lord Shiva exists.

586
01:25:28.550 --> 01:25:30.380
GOVINDA Das: And I experienced them.

587
01:25:31.780 --> 01:25:43.649
GOVINDA Das: And somebody says, I don't believe. So, therefore, we cannot argue in regards to changing somebody else's belief. Based upon experience. We can change their belief based upon some superior logic.

588
01:25:43.650 --> 01:25:55.800
GOVINDA Das: At least at that stage of time. I've got a superior logic, I can defeat, but somebody comes with a superior logic, they can defeat my belief. Therefore, shraddha does not require logic.

589
01:25:55.980 --> 01:26:01.120
GOVINDA Das: Shraddha requires personal conviction. It is subjective.

590
01:26:01.400 --> 01:26:04.270
GOVINDA Das: It exists only if we believe.

591
01:26:05.590 --> 01:26:07.380
GOVINDA Das: And what is Dharma?

592
01:26:07.970 --> 01:26:12.850
GOVINDA Das: I'm supposed to do 3-day seminar on Dharma, the whole subject of Dharma.

593
01:26:13.250 --> 01:26:16.869
GOVINDA Das: Right? Dharma is neutral.

594
01:26:17.280 --> 01:26:20.329
GOVINDA Das: Dharma does not take side.

595
01:26:21.400 --> 01:26:27.709
GOVINDA Das: The Battle of Kurukshetra was based upon Dharma, not based upon Sharadhdha.

596
01:26:28.300 --> 01:26:35.480
GOVINDA Das: Bhishmadev was a great devotee of Krishna, but he was fighting on the side of the Kurus.

597
01:26:36.800 --> 01:26:46.870
GOVINDA Das: Right? And because he was fighting on the side of the Kurus, even though he was a devotee of Krishna, still he had to be punished by the Pandavas.

598
01:26:47.990 --> 01:26:53.389
GOVINDA Das: So he was faithful, but not necessarily taking the side of Dharma.

599
01:26:54.050 --> 01:26:59.070
GOVINDA Das: Therefore, dharma is an inherent order. It's a functional law.

600
01:27:00.100 --> 01:27:05.159
GOVINDA Das: It operates regardless, it does not based upon belief.

601
01:27:05.260 --> 01:27:10.679
GOVINDA Das: I cannot say I don't believe that fire burns. No, it doesn't matter. It will.

602
01:27:10.870 --> 01:27:15.909
GOVINDA Das: You can't say, I don't believe that water quenches my thirst. No, it does.

603
01:27:16.130 --> 01:27:22.440
GOVINDA Das: And therefore, in Sanat and Dharma, when you say, oh, how can somebody die?

604
01:27:22.740 --> 01:27:24.520
GOVINDA Das: How can they die like this?

605
01:27:24.670 --> 01:27:30.109
GOVINDA Das: Death is inevitable, that is part of Dharmic idea.

606
01:27:30.580 --> 01:27:37.160
GOVINDA Das: So, therefore, asking question how this can happen to them, how can they die like that, that is part of life.

607
01:27:38.200 --> 01:27:45.610
GOVINDA Das: Natural is that one lives for 100 years, but there is another naturality of death is it can come anytime.

608
01:27:47.270 --> 01:27:55.609
GOVINDA Das: That is how the depth is defined. So, therefore, it is inherent order of functional law. It does not matter whether you believe or not.

609
01:27:56.920 --> 01:28:04.009
GOVINDA Das: And Satya… As it is a reality, there are things, Dharma, ruthu, and Satya.

610
01:28:04.250 --> 01:28:10.570
GOVINDA Das: Dharma is the functional reality, that means I function based upon truth.

611
01:28:10.770 --> 01:28:14.509
GOVINDA Das: Truth is the invisible reality.

612
01:28:15.050 --> 01:28:25.020
GOVINDA Das: And Rutu is a visible reality. Like, we see, seasons are there. There is Grishma Rutu, Sharad Rutu, there is Varsha Rutu, they're visible.

613
01:28:25.370 --> 01:28:27.460
GOVINDA Das: they're observed.

614
01:28:27.960 --> 01:28:33.160
GOVINDA Das: And beyond their observation, there are subtle laws. Subtle laws are satya.

615
01:28:34.870 --> 01:28:41.519
GOVINDA Das: laws which are visible, that is, Ruthu, and submitting to these two is called as Dharva.

616
01:28:43.310 --> 01:28:54.440
GOVINDA Das: Very simply, we are trying to explain. So therefore, when we practice Dharma, Rituals are based upon Dharma.

617
01:28:55.530 --> 01:29:03.949
GOVINDA Das: sometimes those rituals can go beyond Dharma, based upon willip. Like, somebody told a story.

618
01:29:04.240 --> 01:29:10.199
GOVINDA Das: you know, somewhere in Haridwar, people would come from different parts of India.

619
01:29:10.300 --> 01:29:14.609
GOVINDA Das: to perform the Shradda ceremony for their ancestors.

620
01:29:15.240 --> 01:29:18.140
GOVINDA Das: One man came there, he saw there was a huge crowd.

621
01:29:19.310 --> 01:29:23.909
GOVINDA Das: He took the bath, He collected the water.

622
01:29:24.350 --> 01:29:27.420
GOVINDA Das: He offered it to the… the Surya there.

623
01:29:27.790 --> 01:29:31.730
GOVINDA Das: Then again, you had to go to the water, offer from the inside.

624
01:29:31.940 --> 01:29:37.299
GOVINDA Das: Now, he didn't know where to keep his… his, pot.

625
01:29:38.510 --> 01:29:42.620
GOVINDA Das: What it did was… He put the pod upside down.

626
01:29:43.980 --> 01:29:47.169
GOVINDA Das: And put some sand on it, on the top of the pot.

627
01:29:48.570 --> 01:29:52.500
GOVINDA Das: And he went inside the water. And what happened? People saw that.

628
01:29:52.620 --> 01:29:57.209
GOVINDA Das: And eventually, hundreds of pots were lying there.

629
01:29:58.140 --> 01:30:04.890
GOVINDA Das: You know, in the same fashion. Pot was put upside down, and some sand was placed on it.

630
01:30:05.360 --> 01:30:19.690
GOVINDA Das: Unfortunately, many such belief systems have formed based upon hearsay, based upon blind understanding, and sometimes we try to make that as the

631
01:30:19.790 --> 01:30:20.960
GOVINDA Das: Tradition.

632
01:30:21.320 --> 01:30:25.440
GOVINDA Das: There are many traditions which are blindly practiced.

633
01:30:25.620 --> 01:30:27.360
GOVINDA Das: They need to be questioned.

634
01:30:27.610 --> 01:30:30.949
GOVINDA Das: they need to be put to the test, alright? Because…

635
01:30:31.360 --> 01:30:44.340
GOVINDA Das: They sound ritual, but they're against Dharma. Therefore, shraddha is based upon Dharma. When this indict knowledge, when practices Dharma, Satya, and Trutha.

636
01:30:44.810 --> 01:30:48.679
GOVINDA Das: Then, most of our study of psychology

637
01:30:48.860 --> 01:30:57.599
GOVINDA Das: becomes easy when it is integrated with Dharma, Saty, and Drutta, and helps amazingly for our clients.

638
01:31:05.590 --> 01:31:10.599
GOVINDA Das: Yes. So therefore, this is the verse in the Bhagavatam 3rd Kanto.

639
01:31:11.130 --> 01:31:14.109
GOVINDA Das: Nature and its character remains the same.

640
01:31:14.690 --> 01:31:28.069
GOVINDA Das: This cosmic manifestation is as it is now. It was the same in the past, and it will continue in the same in the future. Sometimes people say, because it is Kaliuga, this is… this is what… how it is.

641
01:31:28.610 --> 01:31:43.959
GOVINDA Das: But if you study the Upanishad, if you study the Puranas also, whether it is Kali, whether it is Threata, whether it is Dhapur, whether it is Saty Yuga, duality was always existing. Hiranne Kashipu was there in Saty Yuga.

642
01:31:44.440 --> 01:31:47.420
GOVINDA Das: Ravan was there in Traitha Yuga.

643
01:31:48.300 --> 01:31:51.429
GOVINDA Das: Duryodhan was there in Dwapar Yuga.

644
01:31:51.590 --> 01:32:05.350
GOVINDA Das: And in Kaliuga, the psychological duryodhans are there, the psychological Ravans are there, the psychological kamsas are there, alright? So the yoga do not change the laws of life.

645
01:32:07.000 --> 01:32:13.750
GOVINDA Das: In Sakti Yuga, maybe people did not drink water when they would travel in a water bottle like this.

646
01:32:14.540 --> 01:32:15.480
GOVINDA Das: Alright?

647
01:32:16.070 --> 01:32:18.569
GOVINDA Das: They did not have this kind of water bottle.

648
01:32:19.060 --> 01:32:23.429
GOVINDA Das: But the concept of drinking was there. Simple example, Bhima.

649
01:32:24.190 --> 01:32:26.439
GOVINDA Das: When he was going with his family.

650
01:32:27.310 --> 01:32:39.739
GOVINDA Das: When Mother Kunti wanted to drink water, he had no pots. There was no running water. What does he do? He takes his utarya, the upper cloth, gets into the river.

651
01:32:40.890 --> 01:32:51.499
GOVINDA Das: cleans the cloth. There was a flowing water, and it dips his cloth inside the water and comes running up and squeezes in the mouth of the mother.

652
01:32:52.400 --> 01:32:54.440
GOVINDA Das: the application changed.

653
01:32:54.730 --> 01:32:57.100
GOVINDA Das: The principle did not change.

654
01:32:57.630 --> 01:33:13.529
GOVINDA Das: Therefore, never, ever give greater emphasis to being, oh, satta Yuga's very good, and kaluyuga bad. No, every yuga has the duality, and that is what this verse is saying.

655
01:33:17.420 --> 01:33:18.210
Dr. Karan Mittal: True.

656
01:33:19.190 --> 01:33:20.210
Dr. Karan Mittal: So…

657
01:33:20.900 --> 01:33:33.719
Dr. Karan Mittal: So if I… if I discuss, or if I look at it from a toolkit perspective as budding counselors, this session gave us two toolkits, like, two things in the toolkit. The first was

658
01:33:33.730 --> 01:33:50.560
Dr. Karan Mittal: whether we bring in faith, spiritual practices, religion, in as a domain in our therapy with a particular client, and it kind of gave us the Jung's perspective that, what are the parameters that will tell you whether the client is using the spiritual belief?

659
01:33:50.560 --> 01:34:03.500
Dr. Karan Mittal: as a performance, or as probably a bypass. So, if a client comes to you, or a counselor comes to you, that's one parameter. The second thing that we saw today in that toolkit was how beliefs

660
01:34:03.500 --> 01:34:13.420
Dr. Karan Mittal: you know, how do we start working with beliefs? So if a person has, like today we saw in one of the breakout rooms, beliefs about spiritual practices, and he's being harsh on himself about

661
01:34:13.530 --> 01:34:24.660
Dr. Karan Mittal: those spiritual practices leading to stress, anxiety, you know, hampering the relationships. So how we dilute those beliefs, how we ask them questions. Of course, it was the first step

662
01:34:24.660 --> 01:34:34.390
Dr. Karan Mittal: Into… into the Sophetic questioning about the beliefs. So we do that, we try to… we don't contradict the beliefs. We don't… we don't directly contradict the beliefs. We…

663
01:34:34.390 --> 01:34:49.419
Dr. Karan Mittal: help them reflect, we help them go deeper, we help them find a source to the belief, and then eventually we give them enough time to reflect and see whether this belief is being functional. Like, most of the people I worked with in the breakout rooms, they had a good part to the belief that it helped them

664
01:34:49.460 --> 01:34:52.169
Dr. Karan Mittal: become what they are today, but it also…

665
01:34:52.220 --> 01:35:05.299
Dr. Karan Mittal: had another dimension that… about stress, about hampering relationships. So we let them, kind of contemplate, and of course, how to work deeper with the beliefs will come later. And now the third part in today's,

