851
01:58:00.330 --> 01:58:04.300
shubham singh: to perform Nishkam Bhav with unattached tendencies.

852
01:58:04.660 --> 01:58:07.580
shubham singh: To come… to bring him out of this tendency.

853
01:58:08.600 --> 01:58:13.300
shubham singh: Or is there any other way we can do? What is your perspective on this?

854
01:58:15.030 --> 01:58:17.479
Dr. Karan Mittal: Provoji, would you like to take the first question first?

855
01:58:17.480 --> 01:58:19.130
GOVINDA Das: You take, you take both, then I'll add.

856
01:58:19.510 --> 01:58:22.620
Dr. Karan Mittal: Yeah, so I think the last question…

857
01:58:22.870 --> 01:58:33.309
Dr. Karan Mittal: If a person thinks about the doership and the ego, etc, you trying to kind of condition him into this nishkam thing also will become a source of his ego.

858
01:58:33.750 --> 01:58:46.480
Dr. Karan Mittal: that I do things, and I'm not attached to the fall of things. So, these are sensitive things. The one thing what we do is, we try to find the source of that tahankar, or that doership.

859
01:58:46.570 --> 01:58:50.420
Dr. Karan Mittal: That is the person trying to fill in the… fill in a vacuum.

860
01:58:50.420 --> 01:59:09.759
Dr. Karan Mittal: by getting egoistic or, you know, claiming leadership and is not able… not… and that's why he's not able to gel with colleagues. So we try to see that, is there any vacuum that he's artificially trying to fill in with this ego and this sense of worship? That is the right approach to kind of dealing with this case. Sometimes what happens is if a person is egoistic, and then you

861
01:59:09.760 --> 01:59:25.880
Dr. Karan Mittal: impose this philosophy of Nishkam, karma, etc. He follows it mechanistically, and this also becomes an added flaw to his ego, that I do things with Nishkam, however, and others do it with, you know, expecting, etc. So it's a very sensitive thing, you have to see.

862
01:59:25.950 --> 01:59:38.659
Dr. Karan Mittal: Where is the vacuum, and which vacuum the client is trying to fill in by claiming this ego. And your Anthataran Chatushta, yes, it can be seen from anything in the world. If you go from the Sankhya philosophy, the world is made from figures.

863
01:59:38.660 --> 01:59:44.779
